    "description": "I was supposed to mint a VeeFriends for my birthday. Had my eye on the Ambitious Angel. Adversity won.\nMonths later, the day before I started radiation & chemo, a tweet about Gary Vaynerchuk\u2019s book reached him directly \u2014 & surrounded by his mother & sister, he spent 20 minutes picking out a World of Women NFT for me.\nVeeFriends has a saying, even made into an enamel pin: \u201cStrangers become acquaintances, acquaintances become friends, friends become family\u201d. The community learned I had cancer, & crowdfunded my 1st VeeCon, the promised utility. The next 2 VeeCon\u2019s acquaintances Zelled me flight money. I sewed an Ambitious Angel costume post surgery & thanks to a Gift Goat holder, I rode a float beside Gary at the 50th Ann. NYC Halloween parade. \nI argue that culture traces directly back to Gary & his mother. It\u2019s what separates a real community from a collectibles market. Takeaway: the most durable utility in Web3 isn\u2019t a roadmap feature \u2014 it\u2019s a culture that turns strangers into family.",
