    "description": "Most NFT projects launched a Discord. Most of those Discords are now silent. The token is still minted, the roadmap still lives, but the community has gone cold. Holders who spent real money want the warmth back.\nHiring community managers doesn\u2019t scale. Generic AI bots read as spam. There\u2019s a third option most projects haven\u2019t tried: building character-driven AI presences that hold the warmth of a community when the humans aren\u2019t there.\nThis talk shares a live proof of concept \u2014 an AI character called Warburton \u2014 running across five platforms (Telegram, X, Instagram, Substack, Spotify) with a consistent fictional universe, multiple named characters, and coherent voice. Built for \u00a3400 in hardware, \u00a320 a month to operate.\nI\u2019ll share what worked, what failed, what the methodology means for NFT holder communities looking for their second wind, and why the universe is the product \u2014 not the bot.",
