    "title": "NFTs Are Not Products: Designing a Relationship Layer for Music",
    "description": "Last year, I shared how music NFTs helped me connect with people around the world, reaching listeners beyond language and culture. This showed me that music NFTs can create global connection.\n\nHowever, I noticed a key issue. Many people discover me through music, not NFTs, and they don\u2019t naturally move into onchain participation. This reveals a gap between music discovery and Web3 engagement.\n\nSo what if the problem is not adoption, but structure?\n\nIn this session, I redefine music NFTs as a relationship layer, not a product. NFTs are not the entry point, but something that comes after emotional connection.\n\nThe framework is simple: Live, Connection, NFT. Live creates emotion, connection builds trust, and NFTs become proof of a shared experience.\n\nI am designing a small experiment around music activities in New York to explore this model.\n\nThis talk focuses on how to build lasting onchain relationships between artists and audiences.",
