    "time": "06:10pm - 06:35pm",
    "room": "Main Stage - Main Ballroom",
    "title": "What Survived the NFT Crash? The Real Value Was Never the Token",
    "description": "What Survived the NFT Crash? The Real Value Was Never the Token\nEveryone remembers the headlines.\n\nThe million-dollar JPEGs. The floor prices. The hype.\n\nBut after the frenzy faded, something unexpected remained.\n\nPeople.\n\nHaving helped moderate and lead communities for some of the largest NFT projects in the space, we've had a front-row seat to the rise, fall, and evolution of Web3 communities. We've watched communities form, grow, fracture, and survive through every stage of the market cycle.\n\nThat experience gave us a unique perspective on something most people missed.\n\nThe most valuable thing created during the NFT era wasn't a token.\n\nIt was the networks, relationships, and opportunities people built together.\n\nThis session explores why some communities thrived while others disappeared, the common mistakes that quietly kill promising projects, and the lessons builders can take from both.\n\nBecause when the charts stop moving, what remains is what mattered all along.",
