    "description": "a day in a phygital environment where NFTs are embedded into everyday life, not as abstract technology, but as functional systems shaping how we move through space.\nFrom the moment a resident wakes up, NFTs operate as:\nAccess keys to physical and digital spaces\nIdentity layers across environments\nPermissions that unlock location-based experiences\nSignals of participation in culture, events, and communities\n\nIn this model, attending underground events, entering private buildings, or accessing hidden layers of the city is no longer controlled by centralized platforms, but by tokenized systems tied to presence and ownership.\n\nAs an architect and XR developer working with real-time environments in Unreal Engine, I design spatial systems where digital ownership directly influences how cities are experienced.\nThis talk translates a speculative future into a practical framework",
