    "title": "From JPEGs to Verifiable NFTs: Secure Reveal, Dynamic Logic & Max Guarantees.",
    "description": "Most NFTs today rely on trust: trust in metadata servers, trust in delayed reveals, trust in off-chain logic. But when NFTs power games, dynamic traits, AI identity, or real-world assets (RWAs), trust is not enough.\n\nThis session introduces a verifiable NFT architecture: NFT (JPEG) + encrypted metadata stored on IPFS + decentralized key reveal.\n\nI'll break down how to design provable reveal mechanics, tamper-resistant dynamic NFTs, and secure tokenized RWAs, without sacrificing decentralization.\n\nThe takeaway: a practical blueprint for building NFTs that don't just look immutable, but are cryptographically accountable.\n\nWhitepaper: https://x.com/datamorpho/status/2036295601218801790",
