    "title": "Beyond Transactions: How Value Flows in NFTs",
    "description": "NFTs introduced new possibilities for ownership, provenance, and creator sovereignty. Yet much of the ecosystem evolved around transactional marketplaces, where value is primarily measured financially.\n\nThis talk explores a different lens: what if value in NFT ecosystems extends beyond transactions, and includes attention, participation, and creative energy, along with relational, emotional, and personal dimensions?\n\nFor platform builders, tokenization projects, and independent artists, this talk examines how incentive structures shape behavior and how current systems optimize for what is easiest to measure: scarcity, rarity, sales, and visibility-driven metrics.\n\nBy introducing the idea of \u201cflow,\u201d it invites a shift toward understanding how value moves through systems, rather than how it is captured. This perspective opens the door to designing NFT ecosystems that are more sustainable, regenerative, and aligned with how people actually create, engage, and connect over time.",
