    "description": "NFTs promised digital ownership\u2014but the reality is more complex.\n\nMost collectors believe they fully own their NFTs. In practice, ownership is shaped by licenses, marketplace rules, and\u2014critically\u2014royalty enforcement mechanisms that remain inconsistent or absent across platforms.\n\nAs marketplaces compete on fees and liquidity, creators are losing control over how their work is monetized and distributed. This raises a fundamental question: if royalties cannot be enforced, what does ownership in NFTs actually mean?\n\nDrawing on experience as a European regulatory lawyer advising Web3 projects, this session explores how legal frameworks, marketplace design, and token models intersect\u2014and what must change to create enforceable, sustainable digital ownership for the next generation of NFT markets.",
