    "description": "Attention is easy to fake. Revenue is not. That's the founding thesis behind LOONY, a protocol that converts verified creator ad revenue into programmatic, on-chain buy pressure instead of tokenizing followers, engagement, or hype. LOONY's beachhead is political and cultural satire, a category with outsized attention, an active creator ecosystem, and no ownership structure built for the people actually making the work. This session breaks down how the mechanism works: creators keep the large majority of their ad revenue, contribute a small negotiated share, and receive a token grant funded by that same contribution, all enforced by smart contract rather than by promise. Attendees will leave with a working framework for telling revenue-backed token mechanics apart from attention-backed ones, and a real-world look at what it means to actually own what you build.",
