    "description": "Italy faces a critical challenge: overtourism chokes iconic cities while hidden villages remain unvisited. In this session, Luca Busolli, Member of the Italian Parliamentary Intergroup on Blockchain, presents \"Smart Heritage,\" a national framework solving this crisis via Web3 and AI.\nSmart Heritage turns passive tourists into active explorers using Experiential NFTs. Acting as digital presence certificates, these NFTs are claimed by scanning physical QR/NFC tags\u2014zero crypto knowledge or apps required.\nThe innovation lies in data governance. An AI analyzes these anonymous check-ins to predict overcrowding 48-72 hours in advance. To prevent congestion, the system uses \"adaptive nudging,\" triggering Flash Missions that reward tourists with rare NFTs and local discounts if they redirect their route to lesser-known areas.\nDiscover how a government-backed blockchain infrastructure can redefine public governance, redistribute economic value, and sustainably preserve cultural heritage",
